ars  went to which experiments they funded at  the wu hun institute of virology  either way this is a total revision of  anthony fauci's position on the subject  it was just a few days ago  that he was incensed he was outraged  morally appalled by the suggestion  that he had funded gain of function  experiments in china  now he's conceding yeah it's totally  possible  but of course he has always known that  it was totally possible  the grant that tony fauci approved for  research at the wuhan lab  explicitly permits gain of function  experiments  in 2014 tony fauci's niaid approved  a grant for a project called  understanding the risk of bat  coronavirus emergence  that project would be run by a group  called eco health alliance  overseen by a man called peter dazek if  that name sounds familiar  that's the same peter daza who spent the  last year telling the world at high  volume  there's no chance this virus escaped  from the web and then  was appointed by the world health  organization to investigate the origins  of kovid  and declared the wuhan lab blameless  what a scam but the grant from fatchi's  nia niaid states that it will fund peter  dasak to quote  test predictions of coronavirus  interspecies transmission predictive  models of host range  i.e emergence potential and will be  tested experimentally using reverse  genetics  pseudovirus and receptor binding assays  and virus infection experiments across a  range of cell  cultures from different species and  humanized mice  oh so actually that's quite a  broad range run that by any scientist  and they will tell you  a lot fits under that description but  specifically  what did those virus infection  experiments with back corona viruses  consist of  precisely well we don't know we have  some idea  seems like maybe the results are all  around us the white house wants you  to calm down they want you know the  intelligence community and no one else  will have to answer  these questions at some point in the  next